From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: well0nez <8986239+well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 18:56:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 16/17] HEVC: hand the entry points of a slice with tiles to
 the decoder

A slice that spans several tiles carries the byte offsets of their
substreams in its header (entry_point_offset_minus1). The driver always
told the kernel num_entry_point_offsets = 0 and never set
V4L2_CID_STATELESS_HEVC_ENTRY_POINT_OFFSETS: VA-API passes the number of
offsets but not the offsets (the subset buffer is optional and was
dropped). cedrus then programs the start and end of the slice's first tile
only and an empty entry point table, so with several tiles in a slice
(kvazaar --tiles, some hardware encoders at 4K) everything after the first
tile decodes wrong or the job times out.

Read the offsets where they are: the slice header the driver parses anyway
for the RPS sizes, continued past them (SAO, reference counts, list
modification, weighted prediction table, QP and deblocking fields) to the
entry points, with the Main and Main 10 syntax. They are handed on only if
that read agrees with what VA-API says about the same slice (slice type,
QP delta, active references, number of offsets), the offsets stay inside
the slice and the decoder's control has room (cedrus: 256); otherwise the
slice goes as before, with one log line. Only pictures with tiles: WPP
streams decode bit-exact without them on cedrus, and stay as they were.

The last tile column and row are now derived from the picture size (6-3,
6-4) instead of copied: VA-API has room for all sizes but the last, a
client may leave that slot empty, and cedrus takes the end of the last
tile from it.

A host test runs the parser over 720 slice NALs with FFmpeg's own header
parser (trace_headers) as the reference: x265 streams with WPP, B-frames
and weighted prediction (the header syntax up to the entry points is the
same as with tiles), Intel tiles streams, and first slices of those
rebuilt bit for bit with 1 and 3 entry points (FFmpeg reads them back as
written). All offsets match, and the RPS sizes it measured before are
unchanged; with the entry points left out, a chroma weight flag loop
dropped or the +1 dropped, it fails.

License: GPL-3.0-or-later, like the code it changes (libva-v4l2_request).
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/codec_hevc.c | 337 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 332 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

